   "provenance": {
    "source_document": "Chen, Krishna, Emer, Sze, IEEE JSSC 52(1), 2017 -- same paper as eyeriss_like",
    "url": "https://eems.mit.edu/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/eyeriss_jssc_2017.pdf",
    "verified": "2026-09-06",
    "inherits": "eyeriss_like",
    "levels": {
     "filter_glb": {
      "quote": "\"Even though it is not required by the dataflow, the remaining 8 kB (two banks of 512-b x 64-b SRAMs) of the GLB is allocated for filter weights to compensate for insufficient off-chip traffic bandwidth. While the PE array is working on a processing pass, the GLB preloads the filters used by the next processing pass.\"",
      "modelled": "depth 1024 (2 x 512), width 64, n_banks 2, datawidth 8 -> 8192 weights",
      "rationale": "The CAPACITY and the BANK GEOMETRY are published exactly; what is a judgement call is whether a double-buffered prefetch store should be declared as a Timeloop reuse level. Modelled as a reuse level here and as !Nothing in eyeriss_like, so the two BRACKET the answer instead of one of them silently choosing it.",
      "why_it_matters": "eyeriss_like refetches resnet18's weights 7.0x from DRAM against 1.0-2.3x for every other design, and the ECC saving is very nearly 0.3125 * E_dram_weights / (total + 0.3125 * E_dram_weights). So this single structural choice sets the largest saving in the study. It is the reason this variant exists."
     }
    }
   }
